# Allowed signers for release tags (ssh-keygen's allowed-signers format; docserver L3, Task 14).
#
# Principal: release-signer. The release workflow (.github/workflows/release.yml, its verify-tag job) runs
#   git -c gpg.format=ssh -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=.github/release-signers verify-tag "$TAG"
# against main's copy of this file, and refuses a tag unless the file holds at least one key line for this principal:
#   release-signer <key type> <public key> [comment]
#
# This file holds no key line yet. The key line is the operator's, supplied for the v1 release; it lands in the v1
# release pull request, beside the change that makes the package public, and never earlier.
# test/public-ready.test.ts (L3.W10) holds that rule: no key line while package.json is private, at least one
# release-signer key line once it is not.
